 :root-cause
 "The warm can? release gate gave the deep generated-authority call graph only 2,000 warmup calls and used one 5,000-call sample median. That is insufficient to reliably separate steady-state service time from HotSpot tiered compilation and shared-runner transitions, so a transient 1,004.339 microsecond result failed the unchanged 1,000 microsecond ceiling even though cold and completed-cache paths passed and fresh local forced authority was materially faster."
 :fix
 "Warm the exact permission-check path for 15,000 calls and gate the median of three independent 5,000-call batch medians. Keep the 1,000 microsecond warm ceiling unchanged so sustained latency across the batches still fails."
